    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.icons\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\n.dockerignore files are misrepresented with the git icon. Similar to the .prettierignore case where the vim api matches it to git ignore.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nSteps to Reproduce\n1. Prerequisites\n\n    A terminal with a Nerd Font installed and configured.\n\n    A recent version of Neovim (v0.9+).\n\n2. Minimal init.lua\n\nCreate a file named minimal_init.lua with the following content. This sets up lazy.nvim and installs only oil.nvim and mini.nvim.\n```\n\n-- bootstrap lazy.nvim\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\n  vim.fn.system({\n    \"git\",\n    \"clone\",\n    \"--filter=blob:none\",\n    \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\n    \"--branch=stable\",\n    lazypath,\n  })\nend\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\n\n-- setup plugins\nvim.api.nvim_set_keymap(\"n\", \"<leader>-\", \"<cmd>Oil<cr>\", { desc = \"Open parent directory\" })\n\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\n  -- Icon provider\n  {\n    \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\n    config = function()\n      require(\"mini.icons\").setup()\n    end,\n  },\n\n  -- File explorer\n  {\n    \"stevearc/oil.nvim\",\n    opts = {\n      view_options = {\n        -- Show hidden files to see .dockerignore\n        show_hidden = true,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n3. Create .dockerignore file and open neovim using the setup\n4. Expected Result\n\nThe .dockerignore file and the Dockerfile should both display the Docker icon (󰡨).\n\n5. Actual Result\n\nThe Dockerfile correctly displays the Docker icon (󰡨).\nThe .dockerignore file incorrectly displays the Git icon (󰊢).",
