            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The same issue I think is still happening with docker-compose.yaml. Oil tries to get using \"file\" and since docker-compose is only identified under filetype it gets the yaml file icon.\n\nThis is *definitely* expected and won't be changed. It is [explicitly not a goal](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c122e852517adaf7257688e435369c050da113b1/doc/mini-icons.txt#L31-L34) for 'mini.icons' to support as much special files cases as possible, which includes config files for all sorts of apps/technologies/languages/etc.\n\nUsers can adjust that by registering custom filetype detection rules (so that 'mini.icons' gets info from that filetype) and/or customize inside `require('mini.icons').setup()`.\n\nSpecifically for 'docker-compose.yml' file, 'mini.icons' [provides special icon data](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c122e852517adaf7257688e435369c050da113b1/lua/mini/icons.lua#L1850), but it indeed requires custom filetype detection. For example, put something like this in the config:\n\n```lua\nvim.filetype.add({\n  filename = {\n    ['docker-compose.yml'] = 'yaml.docker-compose',\n    ['docker-compose.yaml'] = 'yaml.docker-compose',\n  },\n})\n```",
