        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I really think that it should be added as a special file in the firs category here\n\nThe problem is that this file is *not* supported by the `vim.filetype.match()`. This is a hard requirement to limit the amount of supported cases. If it will be supported directly by `vim.filetype.match()`, *then* it can be added to that table.\n\nTo make YAML files not use extension (which is there mostly for speed purposes) and instead rely on `vim.filetype.match()`, configure a dedicated [`config.use_file_extension`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c122e852517adaf7257688e435369c050da113b1/doc/mini-icons.txt#L257-L289). Here is what I use:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.icons').setup({\n  use_file_extension = function(ext, _)\n    local suf3, suf4 = ext:sub(-3), ext:sub(-4)\n    return suf3 ~= 'scm' and suf3 ~= 'txt' and suf3 ~= 'yml' and suf4 ~= 'json' and suf4 ~= 'yaml'\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nTogether with previous `vim.filetype.add`, this works.",
